  "classIri": "urn:ngm:class:archival-node",
  "domain": "blockchain",
  "definition": "An Archival Node is a blockchain network participant that stores the complete historical state of the ledger\u2014every block, transaction, and state root from genesis to the current tip\u2014without pruning older data. Unlike pruned nodes or light nodes, an archival node can respond to queries about any historical state at any block height, making it essential for block explorers, analytics services, and smart contract developers who need point-in-time state access.",
